    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0623" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.248/215: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consul General at Hong Kong</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Southard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-22T16:00:00-05:00">March 22, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. For Lieutenant Colonel Mayer<anchor n="15" xml:id="d647-f1"/> from War
                    Department.</p>
                <p>Your 99, March 15, noon,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d647-f2"/> one hundred American
                    planes are being <pb facs="0624" n="614" xml:id="pg614"/> allotted by the
                    British to China. War Department knows nothing of date of shipment or American
                    pilots. Additional information will be furnished when available.</p>
                <p>Sent to Hong Kong. Repeated to Chungking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
